    "probe": "rave-flyer/v1",
    "of": "examples/probes/rave-flyer.json",
    "target": "Tresor-era Berlin flyer: distorted or stretched display type, a dense information block, one saturated colour on black",
    "method": "the same sheet re-authored against default-v1. The display word is now distorted by the type primitive itself -- anton at stretch [1.45, 2] -- rather than by a stack of 96 translated copies, and the second line is sheared 14 degrees and pulled wide at stretch [1.55, 0.95]. The extrusion survives at a quarter of its old length, doing the job an extrusion actually does, under a screen blend so the copies build up as exposure rather than paint over one another. Cheap reproduction moved off the canvas and into a three-stage print pass.",
    "notDone": "maxTextLength is still 240 and the door-policy copy is 258 characters single-spaced, so the dense block is still two text ops. The gap between them is now an exact multiple of the leading, which is a better fake, not a real one."
  },
